From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:57:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nak: NAK_SCHED_ILP (prepass honors latencies), NAK_FSET_BF,
 NAK_GCM

The prepass places a producer right above its consumer whenever nothing
else is ready. Because its future-ready set uses the graph's static ready
cycle (0), "nothing else" is almost always the case, and the producer is
on the critical path. In 2a040240, 36% of the instructions read the
result of the one before them in the original order and 74% do after the
prepass (reference compiler's code: 2%).

- NAK_SCHED_ILP=1 (default off): an instruction enters the future-ready
  set at the cycle its edge latencies give, as NAK_SCHED_MLP does, with
  the plain latency model (no memory-latency modeling, no hoisting). A
  unit that does not fit its register target keeps the plain schedule.
  The occupancy target is chosen on the plain schedule. Static stall
  cycles with NAK_RA_LRU=1, NAK_SCHED_ILP off -> on: 2a040240 44.4k ->
  39.7k, 88825d04 5.6k -> 5.5k, f125b4a2 770 -> 631, fb2df990
  1585 -> 1502 (40 instead of 48 GPRs, 48 warps instead of 40).
- NAK_FSET_BF=1 (default off): b2f32 of a 32-bit float comparison used
  only there becomes slt/sge/seq/sne (nak_nir_algebraic.py), which
  from_nir.rs emits as one FSET.BF (1.0 or 0.0) instead of FSETP and
  SEL, as in the reference compiler's code. 2a040240: 180 fewer
  instructions.
- NAK_GCM (0-3, default off, fragment shaders only): nir_opt_gcm with
  value numbering after NAK's NIR optimization loop (2: and ALU sunk back
  towards its uses, 3: global loads too). Read-only loads that an
  unrolled loop repeats in each iteration's if become one load in the
  common dominator. While it is on, the occupancy target accepts up to 32
  loop-weighted memory spill operations. Steel Nomad corpus, 136 fragment
  shaders: instructions 133.6k -> 112.4k (-16%), average warps 44.1 ->
  43.4. Lighting FS d2c045ea: 4091 -> 3430 instructions and 312 -> 207 LDGs,
  but 128 GPRs (16 warps) instead of 96 (20 warps), with 16 memory spills.
  The reference compiler uses 128 GPRs for it too.

All three are packed into nak_knobs_key2() (bits 8-11).
